plication factor** by default, rather than inheriting the source topic's replication factor.\\n\\nThis is explicitly stated in a discussion about KIP-1279 (Cluster Mirroring):\\n\\n> \\\"When cluster mirroring creates a topic on the destination, I wonder why it does not inherit the replication factor of the source topic by default. I can understand why you might want source and mirror topics to have different replication factors, but I think the default is currently the default replication factor for the destination cluster, as opposed to the replication factor of the source topic.\\\"\\n\\n**File cited:** `_intake/2026/04/03/mail-3da03c7762b02a3dc6d931ae-3cd2d5a4.md` (lines 67)\\n\\nThis comment from Andrew Schofield raises the observation as a design question during the KIP-1279 discussion thread, noting that while there are valid reasons for allowing different replication factors between source and mirror topics, the current default behavior uses the destination cluster's settings rather than inheriting from the source.\",\"error\":null,\"files\":[\"_intake/2026/04/03/mail-3da03c7762b02a3dc6d931ae-3cd2d5a4.md\"],\"seconds\":17.02,\"truncated\":false,\"turns\":2,\"usage\":{\"cache_read_tokens\":57876,\"cache_write_tokens\":27585,\"cost_usd\":0.0663996,\"input_tokens\":42,\"output_tokens\":1080}}"}}}
